# Feature Folder Structure

Every feature under `lib/features/<feature_name>/` **must** have this exact structure:

```
<feature>/
  data/
    datasources/
      <feature>_remote_data_source.dart       ← abstract interface
      <feature>_remote_data_source_impl.dart  ← Dio implementation, throws on error
    models/
      <model>_model.dart                      ← fromJson + toEntity()
    repositories/
      <feature>_repository_impl.dart          ← try/catch, returns ApiResponse<Entity>
  domain/
    entities/
      <entity>.dart                           ← pure Dart, no JSON, no packages
    repositories/
      <feature>_repository.dart               ← abstract interface only
    usecases/
      <action>_usecase.dart                   ← one class, one call() method
  presentation/
    bloc/
      <feature>_event.dart
      <feature>_state.dart
      <feature>_bloc.dart
    pages/
      <screen>_page.dart
    widgets/
      <component>.dart
```

## Naming Conventions

| Artifact | Convention | Example |
|---|---|---|
| Files | `snake_case.dart` | `auth_repository.dart` |
| Classes | `PascalCase` | `AuthRepositoryImpl` |
| Entities | Singular noun | `User`, `Product` |
| Models | Entity name + `Model` | `UserModel` |
| UseCases | `<Action>UseCase` | `LoginUseCase` |
| DataSources | `<Feature>RemoteDataSource` | `AuthRemoteDataSource` |
| Repositories (interface) | `<Feature>Repository` | `AuthRepository` |
| Repositories (impl) | `<Feature>RepositoryImpl` | `AuthRepositoryImpl` |

## DI — Feature Registration File

Each feature has its own DI file at `core/di/<feature>_injection.dart`.
It is called from the master `core/di/injection.dart`.

```dart
// core/di/injection.dart
Future<void> setupDI() async {
  _setupCore();
  _setupAuth();
  // _setupInventory(); ← add per feature
}
```

## Rules

- A DataSource interface **must** exist alongside its impl — never just the impl
- A Repository interface **must** live in `domain/`, never in `data/`
- Pages go in `pages/`, reusable feature-scoped widgets go in `widgets/`
- Shared/cross-feature widgets go in `core/widgets/`, never in a feature folder
